foundry-emulators-consoles (1.0.5) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Take over mame from foundry-retro-tools. MAME is an emulator and belongs
    in an emulator metapackage; it is also the only packaged coverage of
    discrete-logic PONG, the Magnavox Odyssey, and the Philips Odyssey 2 /
    Videopac G7000 (driver names pong, odyssey, odyssey2, videopac —
    verified against mame 0.285+dfsg1-1 on ubuntu:26.04). Placed in the
    light bucket rather than -heavy so reach and installed size are
    unchanged: foundry-core already pulled mame transitively via
    foundry-retro-tools. mame-tools (chdman, romcmp, unidasm, … — 18.5 MB)
    stays in foundry-retro-tools, where the ROM reverse-engineering
    workflow expects it.

 -- Foundry Linux <packages@foundrylinux.org>  Wed, 05 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

foundry-emulators-consoles (1.0.4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Add ares, sameboy, and mgba-qt (Ubuntu universe). ares closes
    ColecoVision, and also brings MSX/MSX2, SG-1000, Neo Geo Pocket,
    WonderSwan, and Mega Drive/CD/32X. sameboy and mgba-qt add dedicated
    Game Boy family emulators; Game Boy was previously only incidental
    coverage via the multi-system mednafen and mesen2 cores.

 -- Foundry Linux <packages@foundrylinux.org>  Wed, 05 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

foundry-emulators-consoles (1.0.3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Add xemu (Foundry apt), the original Xbox emulator. It is not in Ubuntu
    26.04 universe, so it is packaged by Foundry.
  * Placed here rather than in foundry-emulators-consoles-heavy: the heavy
    bucket's criterion is installation footprint, and xemu measures ~8 MiB
    of marginal dependency closure over the existing light console set
    (libslirp0, libssl3t64, libusb-1.0-0, openssl-provider-legacy) plus a
    ~16 MB binary. See docs/plans/2026-08-05-package-xemu.md.

 -- Foundry Linux <packages@foundrylinux.org>  Wed, 05 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

foundry-emulators-consoles (1.0.2) resolute; urgency=medium

